|~ The verbs of booleans [D62]. Each resides on `::qlang/boolean`, the
   kind whose module declares it [D72]: the negation, and the two
   combinators of conditions, which take booleans [D14]. ~|

:not
  |~~ The negation of a boolean. Null is tested with `eq null`, and a
      subject of another kind is refused.

      ~(false | not | eq true)
      ~(true | not | eq false)
      ~(null | eq null | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:returns ::boolean | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/not})

::NotSubjectNotBooleanError
  |~~ Subject of `not` must be a boolean.
      ~(
        0 | not
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::NotSubjectNotBooleanError ::number]
       )
  ~~|

:and
  |~~ Whether the subject and the right condition both hold, each a
      boolean. Given two conditions, `x | and a b` reads both against
      the subject, the first as the subject of `and` [D72], so it
      composes the clauses of a predicate inside `filter`, `every`
      and `if`.

      ~(true | and false | eq false)
      ~({:active true :age 25} | and /active (/age | gte 18) | eq true)
      ~({:active false :age 25} | and /active (/age | gte 18) | eq false)
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:right ::boolean | :returns ::boolean | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/and})

::AndLeftNotBooleanError
  |~~ The left condition of `and` must answer a boolean.
      ~(
        1 | and true
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::AndLeftNotBooleanError ::number]
       )
  ~~|

::AndRightNotBooleanError
  |~~ The right condition of `and` must answer a boolean.
      ~(
        true | and 1
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::AndRightNotBooleanError ::number]
       )
  ~~|

:or
  |~~ Whether the subject or the right condition holds, each a boolean.
      Given two conditions, `x | or a b` reads both against the
      subject, the first as the subject of `or` [D72].

      ~(false | or true | eq true)
      ~(5  | or (eq 5) (eq 10) | eq true)
      ~(7  | or (eq 5) (eq 10) | eq false)
      ~({:role "admin"} | or (/role | eq "admin") (/role | eq "owner") | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:right ::boolean | :returns ::boolean | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/or})

::OrLeftNotBooleanError
  |~~ The left condition of `or` must answer a boolean.
      ~(
        1 | or true
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::OrLeftNotBooleanError ::number]
       )
  ~~|

::OrRightNotBooleanError
  |~~ The right condition of `or` must answer a boolean.
      ~(
        false | or 1
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::OrRightNotBooleanError ::number]
       )
  ~~|
